briefs.hypothesis:
NOVELTY. It opens a motif family the hall of fame has never tried, the backlit faceplate: one live phosphor screen lies behind the whole page, and the page is a matte slate plate laid over it. Light is seen only where the plate is cut, and the plate is cut only where the machine is live.

It is bred from DISTANT parents, none a neighbour of the leader:
- Glow Ink Zine (r12-wild-1, 4.52, last place, 11.8-12.1 from every carried palette). Its tube glowing up through a hole in the page was named by feedback, soul, style, system and the skeptic as the one idea to keep. Feedback's exact fix: 'a clean bevelled cut-out in slate, with the tube's light spilling onto the cut edge'. Style's note: 'light behind the surface'. It has never been built cleanly.
- Front Panel (r5-idea-2, 7.31). The silk-screened front-panel family did well once and dropped out after round 7. Take its legends set into the rules and its lamps.
- Bench Scope (r10-wild-2, 5.98, 5 promise votes): its civil() and trace() macros for the dial slot.
- Slate Flight Console's annunciator (soul's 'best lamp panel'), used only as the reason a lamp is a hole with light behind it.

It answers the owner's latest word at its root. The carried four bring the original light back as a setting on objects: cases, rails, tubes. Here the original page's whole light (E1-E22) literally is the layer beneath, and every kit effect gets a physical cause:
- 'mind' is stencil-cut through the plate (E1);
- Send is a backlit key whose light pools out of its gap (E3);
- a field lights round its cut edge when opened for typing (E4);
- every lamp is a pinhole (E20);
- the monitors are windows whose light spills onto the bevel and the plate (E12-E17);
- the top afterglow is light leaking under the bar (E6).

Scarcity stops being a style rule and becomes a fact of the object: nothing glows by itself.

It also removes the owner's twice-named 'too-dominant pewter slab'. There are no monitor cases; the plate is the terminal's bezel, extended to the whole page. That is how a real VT100 or 3270 showed its tube, behind a cut in the front.

One rule holds on every page, Plans, To do and Settings included, and the SHAPE of a cut says what it shows:
- a horizontal slot is time;
- a round window is place;
- a square window is Vera;
- a pinhole is live or not.
Where nothing is live, the plate is uncut. That fixes the leader's empty terminal column by construction.

It keeps every usability floor the panel has made a rule.

It is clearly different from the carried four: no docked column or case (Desk Terminal), no banded head column (Traced), no cased instruments over tables (Long Persistence), no track as the page's system (Track Diagram). The expected look-distance is 7 or more from each. It also differs from this round's wild rolls (blueprint, card catalogue, Bauhaus, Tron's glowing outlines), which light the surface itself.
